/*!
@defgroup rcu
@ingroup mod_system Reset Control Unit (RCU)
@brief Reset-source reporting and reset pin filter control module for YTMicro devices.

@details
The Reset Control Unit (RCU) records the cause of the most recent device
reset and provides configuration control for the external RESET_B pin filter
path. The driver exposes a simple singleton API for programming the filter,
reading the raw reset status register, decoding the most common reset sources,
and clearing latched reset flags after they have been processed.

@section rcu_features Key Features
- Configures the external RESET_B digital filter enable state.
- Keeps the reset pin filter active in deep sleep when requested.
- Programs the raw reset pin filter counter value in `RPFR[FLTVAL]`.
- Supports optional reset pin output enable on devices with
  `FEATURE_RCU_HAS_PIN_OUTPUT`.
- Reads the raw reset source status register (`RSSR`) for detailed diagnostics.
- Decodes common single-source reset events into `rcu_reset_reason_t`.
- Clears individual latched reset flags or all currently asserted flags.

@section rcu_standards Supported Reset Sources / Modes

@subsection rcu_standards_sources Supported Reset Sources
| Reset Source | Description | Availability / Driver Mapping |
|--------------|-------------|-------------------------------|
| High-voltage detect | Reset generated by a high-voltage detect event. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_HVD` when `RCU_RSSR_HVD_MASK` exists. |
| Deep-sleep acknowledge timeout | Reset generated when low-power entry acknowledgement does not complete in time. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_DEEPSLEEPACK`. |
| Watchdog | Reset generated by the watchdog on single-core devices. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_WDG` when `NUMBER_OF_CORES == 1`. |
| Watchdog core 0 / core 1 | Per-core watchdog reset reporting on multi-core devices. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_WDG_CORE0` / `RESET_REASON_WDG_CORE1` when `NUMBER_OF_CORES > 1`. |
| Clock monitor | Reset generated when the monitored clock source fails its check. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_CMU`. |
| Core lockup | Reset generated after an unrecoverable core lockup event. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_CORELOCK`. |
| Debug reset | Reset generated by the debug subsystem. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_DEBUG` when `RCU_RSSR_DBG_MASK` exists. |
| Software reset | Reset generated by a software system reset request. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_SOFTWARE_RESET`. |
| External reset pin | Reset generated by asserting the external RESET_B pin. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_PIN`. |
| POR / BOR / LVD | Reset generated during power-on or low-voltage conditions. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_POR_LVD`. |
| FMU fail reaction | Reset generated by the FMU fail-reaction path. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_FMU_FAIL_REACT` when the FMU-related RSSR flag exists. |
| FMU functional reset | Reset generated by the FMU functional reset flag. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_FMU` when the FMU-related RSSR flag exists. |
| Multiple reset sources | More than one `RSSR` flag is latched at the same time. | Reported as `RESET_REASON_MUTI_REASON`. |

@subsection rcu_standards_filter Reset Pin Filter Modes
| Configuration Field | Effect |
|---------------------|--------|
| `pinFilterEnable` | Enables or bypasses the RESET_B digital filter. |
| `pinFilterEnableInDeepsleep` | Keeps the digital filter active while the device is in deep sleep. |
| `filterCount` | Programs the raw debounce/filter count written to `RPFR[FLTVAL]`. |
| `pinOutputEnable` | Enables the optional reset pin output driver when supported by the device. |

@section rcu_arch Module Architecture

The RCU module is organized in a two-layer architecture:

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Application Code                │
│        (calls RCU_DRV_* functions)           │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          RCU Driver Layer (rcu_driver.h/c)   │
│  ● Singleton API for reset pin filter setup  │
│  ● Decodes raw reset status into public enum │
│  ● Clears individual or all RSSR flags       │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│     RCU HW Access Layer (rcu_hw_access.h)    │
│  ● Inline register helpers for RPFR / RSSR   │
│  ● Programs filter bits and write-one-clear  │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│              RCU Hardware Block              │
│     (RESET_B filter control and RSSR latch)  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection rcu_arch_driver Driver Layer (rcu_driver.h)
Application code uses the `RCU_DRV_*` APIs from `rcu_driver.h`. The driver
operates on the singleton `RCU` peripheral base pointer defined by the device
header and does not require an instance index.

@subsection rcu_arch_hw HW Access Layer (rcu_hw_access.h)
This internal layer provides low-level inline register helpers. It is
organized into three functional groups:
- **Reset Pin Filter Control** - `RCU_SetPinFilterCount()`,
  `RCU_EnablePinFilter()`, `RCU_DisablePinFilter()`,
  `RCU_EnablePinFilterInDeepsleep()`, `RCU_DisablePinFilterInDeepsleep()`
- **Reset Pin Output Control** - `RCU_SetPinOutput()` on supported devices
- **Reset Status Register Access** - `RCU_GetResetReasonRawValue()`,
  `RCU_ClearRSSRFlag()`

@section rcu_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection rcu_config_struct rcu_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default Value |
|-------|------|-------------|---------------|
| `pinOutputEnable` | `bool` | Enables the optional reset pin output driver. Present only when `FEATURE_RCU_HAS_PIN_OUTPUT == 1`. | Caller defined |
| `pinFilterEnable` | `bool` | Enables the external RESET_B digital filter. | Caller defined |
| `pinFilterEnableInDeepsleep` | `bool` | Keeps the RESET_B filter active in deep sleep. | Caller defined |
| `filterCount` | `uint8_t` | Raw filter-count value written to `RPFR[FLTVAL]`. | Caller defined |

@subsection rcu_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `FEATURE_RCU_HAS_PIN_OUTPUT` | Enables the `pinOutputEnable` field and the `RCU_SetPinOutput()` helper when the device supports reset pin output control. |
| `NUMBER_OF_CORES` | Selects single watchdog reporting or per-core watchdog reporting in `rcu_reset_reason_t`. |
| `FEATURE_PCTRL_HAS_DIGITAL_FILTER` | Enables FMU-related reset reason enum entries when combined with FMU support. |
| `FMU_INSTANCE_COUNT` | Enables FMU-related reset reason enum entries when at least one FMU instance exists. |

@section rcu_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection rcu_usage_filter Pattern 1: Configure the RESET_B Pin Filter
Use `RCU_DRV_Init()` to apply the desired reset pin filter behavior during
normal run mode and deep sleep.

@code{.c}
rcu_config_t rcuConfig =
{
#if defined(FEATURE_RCU_HAS_PIN_OUTPUT) && (FEATURE_RCU_HAS_PIN_OUTPUT == 1)
    .pinOutputEnable = false,
#endif
    .pinFilterEnable = true,
    .pinFilterEnableInDeepsleep = true,
    .filterCount = 4U
};

RCU_DRV_Init(&rcuConfig);
@endcode

@subsection rcu_usage_decode Pattern 2: Decode the Most Recent Reset Reason
Read the high-level reset reason first when the application only needs the
dominant cause of the most recent reset.

@code{.c}
rcu_reset_reason_t reason;

reason = RCU_DRV_GetResetReason();

switch (reason)
{
#if defined(NUMBER_OF_CORES) && (NUMBER_OF_CORES > 1U)
case RESET_REASON_WDG_CORE0:
case RESET_REASON_WDG_CORE1:
#else
case RESET_REASON_WDG:
#endif
    /* Recover from a watchdog reset. */
    break;
case RESET_REASON_PIN:
    /* External reset pin assertion. */
    break;
case RESET_REASON_MUTI_REASON:
    /* Fall back to raw RSSR inspection for multi-source cases. */
    break;
default:
    /* Handle other reset causes as needed. */
    break;
}
@endcode

@subsection rcu_usage_raw Pattern 3: Inspect and Clear Raw Reset Flags
Use the raw `RSSR` value when the application needs to inspect multiple
latched reset sources before clearing them.

@code{.c}
uint32_t rawFlags;

rawFlags = RCU_DRV_GetResetReasonRawValue();

if ((rawFlags & RCU_RSSR_PIN_MASK) != 0U)
{
    RCU_DRV_ClearResetReasonFlag(RESET_REASON_PIN);
}

if (RCU_DRV_GetResetReason() == RESET_REASON_MUTI_REASON)
{
    /* Clear every currently latched flag after logging the raw value. */
    RCU_DRV_ClearResetReasonFlag(RESET_REASON_MUTI_REASON);
}
@endcode

@section rcu_api API Quick Reference

@subsection rcu_api_init Initialization
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `RCU_DRV_Init()` | Apply reset pin filter and optional pin output settings. |

@subsection rcu_api_query Reset Reason Query
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `RCU_DRV_GetResetReason()` | Decode the latched reset source into `rcu_reset_reason_t`. |
| `RCU_DRV_GetResetReasonRawValue()` | Read the raw `RSSR` register value for detailed diagnostics. |

@subsection rcu_api_clear Reset Reason Flag Management
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `RCU_DRV_ClearResetReasonFlag()` | Clear the selected latched reset flag or all flags when `RESET_REASON_MUTI_REASON` is used. |

@section rcu_notes Important Notes

@subsection rcu_notes_multi Multi-Source Reset Handling
@note `RCU_DRV_GetResetReason()` only reports a single decoded value. When
multiple `RSSR` bits are set, the driver returns `RESET_REASON_MUTI_REASON`.
Call `RCU_DRV_GetResetReasonRawValue()` to inspect the individual flags.

@subsection rcu_notes_clear Write-One-To-Clear Behavior
@warning `RCU_DRV_ClearResetReasonFlag()` clears flags through a
write-one-to-clear update of `RSSR`. Passing `RESET_REASON_MUTI_REASON`
clears every flag that is currently latched.

@subsection rcu_notes_filter Reset Pin Filter Programming
@warning `filterCount` is written directly to `RPFR[FLTVAL]` without range
checking. Choose a device-appropriate value before calling `RCU_DRV_Init()`.

@subsection rcu_notes_optional Optional Device Features
@note `pinOutputEnable` is only available on devices that define
`FEATURE_RCU_HAS_PIN_OUTPUT == 1`. FMU-related reset reasons are only
reported when the corresponding device-specific RSSR flags exist.

@section rcu_integration Integration Guide

@subsection rcu_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source file must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/rcu/rcu_driver.c
@endverbatim

@subsection rcu_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directory to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
@endverbatim

@subsection rcu_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No special compile-time symbols are required for this module. Device-specific
feature macros such as `FEATURE_RCU_HAS_PIN_OUTPUT` and `NUMBER_OF_CORES`
come from the selected device header.

@subsection rcu_integration_deps Dependencies
- No additional driver-module dependencies are required beyond the selected
  device header and the standard SDK driver include path.

*/
